invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: rsa_vp1_cpu hands rsa_ifma_public 2^(52n) mod m in place of
  2^(104n) mod m, which is R' rather than R'^2, so the first product
  writes the base itself and every result is off by a power of R'.
  bin/rsa_ifma_model_test compiles rsa_mont.c's dispatch over the lane
  model and compares rsa_vp1_cpu under the bit with rsa_vp1.

--- old
        power_of_two_mod(digit_r2, mod.m, k, 104 * rsa_ifma_digit_count(k));
--- new
        power_of_two_mod(digit_r2, mod.m, k, 52 * rsa_ifma_digit_count(k));
